#
# Counter-example for lang:FlagshipScenarioShape: a lang:FlagshipScenario that declares
# its worked example, its competency question, and its counter-example but OMITS
# lang:enforcesFailureClass (sh:minCount 1), so validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent (and no other finding). The other three links are
# present so ONLY the missing-enforcing-failure-class violation fires, isolating it — an
# acceptance scenario whose gate raises no named failure is unwired
# (lang:UnwiredFlagshipScenario).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecFlagshipUnwired).
@prefix lang: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/lang/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/lang/> .

ex:unwiredScenario a lang:FlagshipScenario ;
    lang:demonstratedByExample "tests/conformance-fixtures/meaning-cats-chase-mice.ttl" ;
    lang:demonstratedByCompetency <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/lang/tests/cqDenotationsToFormula> ;
    lang:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/meaning-underspecified-denotation.ttl" .
